======================================================================================
CHECK C - CONNECTIVITY SCENARIOS: WHAT DOES THE DRAWN RADIUS MEAN?
======================================================================================
  quality(d) = peak * exp(-0.5 d^2/(radius/2)^2)
    at d = radius      -> exp(-2) = 13.5% of peak  (what the circle shows)
    delivery prob 0.5  -> d ~ 0.57 * radius for a strong region
  Gilbert-Elliott mean multiplier = 0.768, so effective p = q * 0.768

  conn      geometric>0.5  effective>0.5  inside drawn circle
  sparse            24.8%          13.1%                63.6%
  dense             52.7%          31.4%                98.6%

  => the drawn circles overstate real coverage by roughly 3-5x.

